  "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThis sample protocol outline is for demonstration purposes only. It does not report completed research or real results.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EObjective\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETo assess whether digital self-management interventions improve clinical and patient-reported outcomes for adults with heart failure compared with usual care.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EEligibility Criteria\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EPopulation:\u003C/strong\u003E Adults aged 18 or over with a clinician-confirmed diagnosis of heart failure\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EIntervention:\u003C/strong\u003E Mobile apps, telemonitoring, web-based education or other digital tools that support self-management\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EComparator:\u003C/strong\u003E Usual care or a non-digital active control\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EOutcomes:\u003C/strong\u003E The primary outcome is heart failure readmission. Secondary outcomes include all-cause readmission, mortality, quality of life, self-care behaviour, medication adherence, usability and adverse events.\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cstrong\u003EStudy design:\u003C/strong\u003E Randomised controlled trials\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Ch2\u003ESearch Strategy\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EMEDLINE, Embase, CINAHL and the Cochrane Central Register of Controlled Trials would be searched from database inception. Trial registers and reference lists would also be checked. The protocol would be registered with PROSPERO, and reporting would follow PRISMA 2020.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EStudy Selection and Data Extraction\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ETwo reviewers would independently screen studies and extract data, resolving disagreements through discussion or a third reviewer. Extracted data would include participant characteristics, intervention features, follow-up duration and outcomes.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EQuality Assessment\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003ERisk of bias would be assessed using the Cochrane RoB 2 tool. Certainty of evidence would be assessed using GRADE.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EData Synthesis\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EWhere studies are sufficiently similar, a random-effects meta-analysis would be conducted. Dichotomous outcomes would be reported as risk ratios and continuous outcomes as mean differences or standardised mean differences. Heterogeneity would be assessed using the I\u003Csup\u003E2\u003C/sup\u003E statistic. Planned subgroup analyses include intervention type, heart failure phenotype and follow-up duration. If pooling is inappropriate, a structured narrative synthesis would be used.\u003C/p\u003E"
}]]></Value>
